--TEST--
A `use` that does not resolve reports once, at the `use` line, and each later use of its short name as a type, in `new`, in a static call, in `extends` and in a `catch` reports nothing — `rule:types/one-mistake-reports-once`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

// Nothing declares `App\Missing`. Its error is the only one this file gives.
use App\Missing;

// `extends Missing` gives no error.
class Shop extends Missing {
}

class Store {
    // A parameter typed `Missing` and a property read on it give no error.
    public static function label(Missing $item): string {
        string $name = $item->name;
        return $name;
    }

    // `new Missing()` and the static call `Missing::build()` give no error.
    public static function make(): void {
        Missing $made = new Missing();
        Missing $built = Missing::build();
    }

    // `catch (Missing $e)` gives no error.
    public static function guard(): void {
        try {
            Store::make();
        } catch (Missing $e) {
        }
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0306]: `App\Missing` does not resolve to any declaration
  --> %s:5:5
  |
5 | use App\Missing;
  |     ^^^^^^^^^^^ no matching class, interface or enum declared

error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
